# Spartan — Rules & Standards

## Identity
Custom lightweight PHP 8.1+ MVC framework. Zero external dependencies in core. Composer packages are allowed when needed.
**Never assume Laravel/Symfony/Yii conventions. Everything below is the law.**

---

## Absolute Prohibitions

| Forbidden | Use Instead |
|---|---|
| `$_GET`, `$_POST`, `$_FILES`, `$_SESSION`, `$_SERVER` in Controllers/Models | `$this->request->*`, `$this->session->*` |
| `header("Location: ...")`, `http_response_code()` | `$this->redirect()`, `$this->response->setStatusCode()` |
| Raw `echo $var`, `<?= $var ?>` without escaping | `{{ $var }}` / `@escape($var)` / `$this->escape($var)` |
| SQL strings inside Controllers or Views | All SQL stays in Models via `$this->table()->...` |
| `Application::$app->db`, models, or any DB call inside View files | Pass data from Controller via `$this->render('view', ['key' => $value])` |
| Hardcoded paths, credentials, or env-specific values | `.env` → `config/config.php` → `Application::$app->config` |
| `session_start()` manually | Session auto-starts in `Session::__construct()` |
| `isset()`/`empty()`/`filter_var()` validation chains in Controllers | `$this->validate($data, $rules)` |
| `view()`, `request()`, `redirect()`, `env()`, `config()` helpers | Not defined — do not use |
| Implicit table names or auto-resolved foreign keys | Always declare `$table`, `foreignKey`, and relation `as:` explicitly |
| Third-party namespaces (Carbon, Illuminate, etc.) | Native PHP unless explicitly instructed |
| DDL queries (`ALTER`, `CREATE`, `DROP`) inside Controllers | `database/migrations/` sequenced files via `php spartan migrate` |
| Manual `session_write_close()` in Controllers | Spartan auto-releases session lock at end of `Application::run()` |

---

## Structure

```
config/config.php          ← env loader, returns config array
public/index.php           ← front controller only (loads routes, runs app)
routes/web.php             ← public pages
routes/admin.php           ← protected pages
routes/api.php             ← JSON endpoints
src/Controllers/           ← extend Spartan\Controller
src/Models/                ← extend Spartan\Model
src/Views/                 ← .blade.php (preferred) or .php (fallback)
src/Views/layouts/         ← layout wrappers
src/Middlewares/           ← extend Spartan\Middleware
src/Services/              ← business logic, no extends required
src/Listeners/             ← must implement handle(mixed $payload): void
src/Events/                ← event name constants
framework/src/             ← the spartan/framework package (namespace Spartan\, do not modify unless requested)
database/migrations/       ← sequenced .sql files
storage/logs/              ← daily log files (auto-created)
storage/cache/             ← file cache (auto-created)
```

---

## Coding Rules

- `declare(strict_types=1);` at the top of every PHP file — no exceptions.
- Namespace matches folder: `src/Controllers/` → `namespace App\Controllers;`
- One class per file. PSR-4 autoloading via Composer or built-in fallback.
- Code to interfaces: use `SessionInterface`, `ViewInterface`, `AuthInterface` — not concrete classes.
- Action methods return `string` (rendered HTML) or `void` (redirect/JSON).

---

## Controllers

```php
// Inject via constructor (container auto-resolves)
class OrderController extends Controller {
    public function __construct(private PaymentService $payment) {
        parent::__construct();
    }
}

// Available in every controller action:
$this->request       // Request object
$this->response      // Response object
$this->session       // SessionInterface
$this->auth          // AuthInterface

// Shortcuts:
$this->render('view_name', $data);          // full page
$this->renderViewOnly('partial', $data);    // HTMX partial — no layout
$this->redirect('/path');
$this->json(['key' => 'value']);
$this->make(SomeService::class);
$this->event('order.placed', $payload);
$this->share('key', $value);               // share to all views
```

---

## Request

```php
$this->request->get('key')       // $_GET
$this->request->post('key')      // $_POST or JSON body
$this->request->input('key')     // POST → GET fallback
$this->request->getParam('key')  // unified alias for input()
$this->request->getBody()        // all inputs as array
$this->request->file('avatar')   // uploaded file metadata
$this->request->header('Authorization')
$this->request->isAjax()
$this->request->isPost()
```

Upload path: `Application::$app->config['storage']['uploads']` — never hardcode.

```php
// UploadedFile — safe Unicode/Arabic filename handling
$file = $this->request->upload('document');  // returns UploadedFile or null
if ($file && $file->isValid()) {
    $file->getOriginalName();   // 'برسم المصحف.pdf' — full UTF-8 preserved
    $file->hashName();          // 'a3f7c91b...8f1a.pdf' — safe random name
    $file->sanitizedName();     // 'برسم_المصحف.pdf' — cleaned but readable
    $file->store(Paths::storage('uploads'));
}
// Legacy: $this->request->file('key') still returns raw ?array
```

---

## Models & QueryBuilder

> **NEVER write raw SQL strings inside model methods — use QueryBuilder exclusively.**  
> **NEVER access `$table` property directly from outside the model. Always call `$model->getTable()`.**

```php
class Product extends Model {
    protected string $table = 'products';
    protected bool $timestamps = true;  // auto created_at / updated_at
}

// QueryBuilder — always via $this->table()
$this->table()->get();
$this->table()->where('active', 1)->first();
$this->table()->find($id);                        // raw array
(new Product)->findInstance($id);                 // hydrated Model
(new Product)->findInstanceBy('slug', $slug);
$this->table()->where('status', 'paid')->count();
$this->table()->where('active', 1)->exists();
$this->table()->where('role', ['a','b'], 'IN')->get();
$this->table()->select('id', 'name')->orderBy('name', 'DESC')->limit(10)->offset(0)->get();
$this->table()->groupBy('status')->having('cnt', 5, '>=')->get();
$this->table()->paginate(15, $page);   // returns ['data','total','per_page','current_page','last_page']

// Write (require at least one where() — throws LogicException otherwise)
$this->table()->insert(['col' => 'val']);         // returns last insert ID
$this->table()->where('id', $id)->update($data);  // returns affected rows
$this->table()->where('id', $id)->delete();       // returns deleted rows
$this->table()->truncate();                       // intentional full clear

// Timestamps shortcuts (auto-injects created_at / updated_at when $timestamps = true)
$this->create($data);
$this->save($id, $data);

// Joins
$this->table('orders')
     ->join('users', 'orders.user_id', 'users.id')               // standard
     ->leftJoin('coupons', 'orders.coupon_id', '=', 'coupons.id') // with operator
     ->join('logs', 'logs.order_id = orders.id AND logs.active = 1') // raw ON
     ->select('orders.id', 'users.name')
     ->get();

// Transactions (auto commit/rollback)
$this->transaction(function ($model) {
    $model->table('orders')->insert([...]);
    $model->table('invoices')->insert([...]);
});

// Global transactions (multi-model, no model instance needed)
Database::transaction(function (\PDO $db) {
    (new Order)->create([...]);
    (new Invoice)->create([...]);
    (new Notification)->create([...]);
});

// toArray
$model->toArray();  // returns $attributes as plain array
```

---

## Relationships

```php
// Define in Model
public function orders(): RelationQuery { return $this->hasMany(Order::class, foreignKey: 'user_id'); }
public function profile(): RelationQuery { return $this->hasOne(Profile::class, foreignKey: 'user_id'); }
public function user(): RelationQuery   { return $this->belongsTo(User::class, foreignKey: 'user_id'); }

// Single record
$orders = (new User)->orders()->for($user);    // array
$user   = (new Order)->user()->for($order);    // array or null

// Eager load — 2 queries total, never N+1
$users = (new User)->orders()->loadFor($users, as: 'orders');
$orders = (new Order)->user()->loadFor($orders, as: 'user');
// ❌ NEVER call for() inside a foreach loop
```

---

## Validation

```php
$v = $this->validate($this->request->getBody(), [
    'email'    => 'required|email|unique:users,email',
    'password' => 'required|min:8|max:64',
    'phone'    => 'nullable|string|min:7',
    'slug'     => 'required|regex:/^[a-z0-9-]+$/',
]);
if ($v->fails()) {
    return $this->render('form', ['errors' => $v->errors()]);
}
```

Rules: `required`, `string`, `integer`, `boolean`, `numeric`, `email`, `url`, `date`, `alpha`, `alpha_num`, `min:N`, `max:N`, `confirmed`, `in:a,b,c`, `nullable`, `regex:/pattern/`, `unique:table,column`

Every form view MUST display validation errors when present.

### FormRequests (encapsulate validation + authorization)

When a controller action has complex validation, extract it into a `FormRequest` under `src/`:

```php
namespace App\Controllers\Requests;
use Spartan\FormRequest;

class StorePostRequest extends FormRequest {
    public function authorize(): bool {
        return $this->session->get('role') === 'admin';
    }
    public function rules(): array {
        return ['title' => 'required|string|min:5|max:100'];
    }
}

// Controller — router auto-instantiates, validates, and injects:
public function store(StorePostRequest $request) {
    $data = $request->getBody(); // only reaches here if valid
}
// If validation fails → auto-redirect with flashed errors (HTML) or 422 (AJAX)
```

---

## Session & Auth

```php
$this->session->set('key', $value);
$this->session->get('key');
$this->session->regenerate();        // REQUIRED after login or privilege change
$this->session->setFlash('status', 'Saved!');

// Auth (AuthInterface)
$this->auth->check();   // bool
$this->auth->id();      // user ID
$this->auth->user();    // hydrated User model or null
```

---

## Routes

```php
// routes/web.php — public
$app->router->get('/', [HomeController::class, 'index']);
$app->router->post('/contact', [HomeController::class, 'contact']);
$app->router->get('/item/{id}', [ItemController::class, 'show']);

// routes/admin.php — protected
$app->router->get('/admin', [AdminController::class, 'index'], ['admin_auth']);

// Middleware groups
$app->router->middlewareGroup('admin_auth', [SecurityHeadersMiddleware::class, AuthMiddleware::class]);

// CSRF exclusions (webhooks, stateless API)
$app->router->excludeCsrf('/api/webhook', '/api/v1/*');

// Method spoofing (forms are GET/POST only)
// <input type="hidden" name="_method" value="DELETE">

// Route redirects
$app->router->redirect('/old-path', '/new-path');         // 302 temporary
$app->router->redirect('/legacy', '/modern', 301);       // 301 permanent

// Fallback handler (catches all unmatched routes before 404)
$app->router->fallback([FallbackController::class, 'handle']);
```

---

## Middlewares

```php
// Create in src/Middlewares/, extend Spartan\Middleware
class MyMiddleware extends Middleware {
    public function execute(Request $request, Response $response): void { ... }
}

// Register on route
$app->router->get('/path', [Controller::class, 'action'], [MyMiddleware::class, 'rate_limit:60,60']);
```

---

## Views (Blade preferred)

```blade
@extends('layouts.main_blade')
@section('content')
    <p>{{ $name }}</p>         {{-- auto-escaped --}}
    {!! $safeHtml !!}          {{-- raw — only when explicitly safe --}}
    @escape($var)
    @csrf                      {{-- required in every POST form --}}
    @flash('status')
    @if($authUser) ... @endif
    @can('edit', $post) ... @endcan
    @role('admin') ... @endrole
    @include('partials.card', ['item' => $item])
@endsection
```

Native PHP templates: use `$this->escape($var)` and `<?= $this->csrfToken() ?>`.  
HTMX partials: use `$this->renderViewOnly(...)` — never return full layout.

---

## Events & Listeners

```php
// Register (in routes/ or boot file)
Application::$app->events->listen('order.placed', UpdateInventory::class);           // sync
Application::$app->events->listen('order.placed', SendSms::class, async: true, maxAttempts: 3, onFailure: 'retry');

// Dispatch from Controller
$this->event('order.placed', $orderData);

// Listener class
class SendSms {
    public function handle(mixed $payload): void { ... }
}
```

Side effects (SMS, email, HTTP calls, file generation) → always async.

---

## Cache

```php
$data = Cache::remember('key', 3600, fn() => $this->table()->get());
Cache::put('key', $value, 600);
Cache::get('key', 'default');
Cache::forget('key');
Cache::flush();
```

Default: file driver. Switch: `CACHE_DRIVER=redis` in `.env`.

---

## Authorization (RBAC)

```php
// Attributes on controller or method
#[RequireRole('admin')]
#[RequirePermission('publish_post')]

// Gate
Gate::define('edit-settings', fn($user) => $user->hasRole('admin'));
Gate::allows('edit-settings');
Gate::denies('edit-settings');
Gate::policy(Post::class, PostPolicy::class);

// User model (HasAuthorization trait)
$user->hasRole('admin');
$user->hasPermission('publish_post');
$user->assignRole('editor');
```

---

## CLI

```bash
php spartan migrate       # run pending migrations
php spartan db:seed       # seed database
php spartan worker        # process job queue (single pass)
php spartan worker --loop # process job queue (daemon, every 5s)
```

---

## Logger

```php
Application::$app->logger->info("User {id} logged in", ['id' => $userId]);
Application::$app->logger->error("Payment failed", ['order' => $orderId]);
// Levels: debug, info, notice, warning, error, critical, alert, emergency
// Output: storage/logs/app-YYYY-MM-DD.log (rotates at 10MB)
```

---

---

## Feature Addition Workflow (mandatory order)

When adding any feature, follow this layer order — **never skip or merge layers**:

```
1. routes/       → Register route + attach middlewares
2. src/Models/   → Add/update model and DB queries (QueryBuilder only)
3. src/Services/ → If business logic spans multiple models or has side effects
4. src/Controllers/ → Orchestrate: receive input → call model/service → dispatch events → return view/json
5. src/Views/    → Present data only — zero logic, zero DB access
```

> Business logic in Controllers = spaghetti.  
> DB queries in Controllers or Views = hard veto.  
> Side effects inline in Controllers (SMS, email, inventory) = must be a Listener instead.

---

## Security Checklist

- [ ] `declare(strict_types=1)` in every file
- [ ] All output in views is escaped
- [ ] Every POST form has `@csrf`
- [ ] `session->regenerate()` called after login
- [ ] No hardcoded credentials or paths
- [ ] Validation runs before any DB write
- [ ] `APP_DEBUG=false` in production `.env`
- [ ] Upload path from config, not hardcoded
- [ ] No user input passed directly to `$this->render()` or `$this->redirect()`
